# oracle: compute pe/atom and stress/atom (kspace terms) with coul/long/dielectric 8.0 and pppm/dielectric (as w243de_efield_kspace_kw_pppm), per-atom values dumped; native's per-atom pppm/dielectric energy and virial come from the scaled-charge mesh with the unscaled charges, so they do not sum to elong and the virial
# Measured max relative error, engine vs native (thermo rows, final atoms): thermo 8.2e-10, atoms 3.2e-9 (the per-atom kspace energy and virial; the pppm/dielectric FFT summation order).
# oracle-inputs: w226cs_diel.data
# oracle-files: w268pd_diel_peratom.dump
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all rel=1e-8 abs=1e-12 filerel=1e-8
units           real
atom_style      dielectric
read_data       w226cs_diel.data
pair_style      coul/long/dielectric 8.0
pair_coeff      * *
bond_style      harmonic
bond_coeff      1 100.0 1.5
special_bonds   lj/coul 0.0 0.5 1.0
kspace_style    pppm/dielectric 1.0e-5
compute         pa all pe/atom kspace
compute         sa all stress/atom NULL kspace
thermo_style    custom step pe ecoul elong evdwl press
thermo_modify   format float %.15g
dump            d all custom 1 w268pd_diel_peratom.dump id c_pa c_sa[1] c_sa[2] c_sa[3] c_sa[4] c_sa[5] c_sa[6]
dump_modify     d sort id format float %.15g
run             0
